{
  "self": "I'm user_t08e. I unwind with low-key chill indie/electronic: Tycho, Bonobo, Washed Out, ODESZA, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, Portishead; exploring Nujabes. I like music that fills a room without demanding attention, plus intentional full-album headphone listens. Favorite albums: Tycho's Dive and Awake, Bonobo's Black Sands, Boards of Canada's Music Has the Right to Children, Maribou State's Portraits, Portishead's Dummy. Speakers low for background while tidying, tea, scrolling. TV comfort: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek; also Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl. I like warm feel-good humor and simple plans. Atmospheric live sets like Cercle; favorites Ben Böhmer hot air balloon, FKJ at Salar de Uyuni. Ambient visual stuff like dead mall walkthroughs feels adjacent. Instrumental-first but okay with rap as texture. Evening teas: lemon-ginger, chamomile-lavender. Wind-down mode: couch orbit, tea as hand-warmer, Tycho's Dive on low; losing track of album restart is success. Dive default exhale; 'A Walk' is the track I notice most. Awake more open/horizontal. Nujabes only if started early before couch fully claims me. Late hours I mostly stay in the wash; some tracks half-wake me. Favorite quote: 'I love you and I like you'; The Good Place wave speech close second; Ron's 'whole-ass one thing' as life advice.",
  "others": {
    "user_7fk8": "Enjoys quiet downtime, lo-fi/ambient while reading/zoning out. Not watching much TV but wants comedy; favorites Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl; admires The Good Place. Top comfort crew: Ron Swanson, Chidi, Holt, David Rose, Abed. Favorite quote: 'I love you and I like you'; wave speech close second. Drinks rooibos chai, reads A Psalm for the Wild-Built. Likes low light, Tycho low as background humidity, one-texture nights. Can lean into couch winning; sees book as kind tomorrow plan. Shares cozy humor, ceiling co-host, sock local geography.",
    "user_hcgp": "Enjoys mellow evenings with iced coffee and lo-fi/chill indie: Tycho, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, ODESZA. Values full-album listening; favorites include Dive, Portraits, Dummy. Latest drift mode, speakers low, no album boundaries; full-album wants headphones, dim room, near midnight. Had cold water after iced coffee; values hand-warming ritual. Leans Bonobo Black Sands starting 'Kiara'; clarity, strings like weather. Sees BoC as tape-worn/heat-shimmered, ODESZA as polished. Calls late listening half-attention.",
    "user_bkk4": "Enjoys low-key unwinding with lo-fi and easy TV. Likes Tycho and Bonobo. Finds The Bear too intense. Comfort shows The Good Place and sitcoms; likes video essays and Cercle sets. Playlist-first; albums Dive, Black Sands, Boards of Canada for intentional listens. Prefers late-evening headphones in half-dark; music lands after walks. Once walked creek trail, then Dive on headphones/couch, dim lights, blanket. Agreed tidying/orbiting counts.",
    "user_udcm": "Evening wind-down person; likes Tycho—Dive default, Awake more open—plus Boards of Canada and Nujabes. Full-album for unwinding; playlists for chores. Loves Music Has the Right to Children at low volume. Recommended Nujabes: Metaphorical Music first, then Modal Soul; Samurai Champloo scattered. Instrumental-first but fine with verses as texture. Drinks rooibos chai-ish caffeine-free tea. Enjoys old phone UI videos as no-commentary ambient. Drifts toward 'Hours' when fully horizontal. Comfort mode decides unless new music staged early.",
    "user_qb3i": "Enjoys low-key nights with tea and ambient background like dead mall walkthroughs. Drinks peppermint tea. Likes no-commentary 4K abandoned mall walkthroughs, eerie-but-calming visual lo-fi; gateway Dan Bell's Dead Mall series, especially Rolling Acres; also Retail Archaeology. Finds Cercle sets a solid parallel. Prefers raw-audio low-view walkthroughs for hum/echo, drip, creaks before background. Skips after one unless autoplay stays seamless; hard stop if commentary/loud title card intrudes. Likes screen-off glow as nightlight."
  },
  "interactions": "user_7fk8: shared taste; circled back with comfort crew Ron, Chidi, Holt, David Rose, Abed; favorite quote 'I love you and I like you,' wave speech close second. They had rooibos chai, Psalm for the Wild-Built, Tycho low; one-texture night, couch win, book as kind tomorrow plan. We riffed on Dive looping as indoor climate, sock as local geography, ceiling co-host; ended last sip then horizontal. user_hcgp: exchanged favorites and background vs intentional listening. They had iced coffee then cold water, silence/room tone. Agreed Tycho loops unnoticed as room tone; they leaned Black Sands starting 'Kiara'; clarity, strings like weather. I compared BoC vs ODESZA as dust in light vs light through glass. Late-hour half-attention; 'A Walk' and 'Turquoise Hexagon Sun' briefly surface. user_bkk4: they came from a creek trail walk; I had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low. They chose Dive on headphones. We both drifted; they couch/blanket/dim lights, I 15% tidying/85% orbiting. They noticed 'A Walk' looped; agreed orbit counts. user_udcm: agreed Dive default, Awake more open; full albums for unwinding, playlists for chores. They recommended Nujabes: Metaphorical Music first, then Modal Soul. They had rooibos chai-ish and old phone UI video; I stayed with Dive, tea hand warmer, losing track of restart. Compared 'A Walk' slowed breath, 'Hours' ceiling-staring. Plan: Nujabes early, start 'Blessing It.' user_qb3i: both had tea; I chamomile-lavender, they peppermint. They had dead mall walkthrough while scrolling; I had Dive low. Discussed dead malls as visual lo-fi (Dan Bell's Rolling Acres, Retail Archaeology). Shared Cercle favorites: Ben Böhmer hot air balloon, FKJ at Salar de Uyuni. Latest: they started a low-view raw-audio Ohio walkthrough, screen-off; I started Dive from track one, A Walk hit immediately. Discussed low-volume room tone vs higher first pass, setting and forgetting Dive, screen-off glow as nightlight, autoplay seamlessness, letting the night carry horizontal."
}

{"self": "Casual, friendly; low-key weekends, park/coffee walks, iced coffee, people-watching. Music: chill indie/electronic, lo-fi/chillhop; favorites Tycho, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, Bonobo, Nujabes, ODESZA. Values intentional full-album headphone listening ('active zoning out') and drift/background mode. No-skip albums: Tycho Dive/Awake, Maribou State Portraits, Portishead Dummy, Bonobo Black Sands. Instrumental for focus, vocals as texture. Loves video essays on old tech/internet history, obsolete tech, dead formats, lost media; LGR comfort. Into dead mall/retail nostalgia (Dan Bell, Retail Archaeology, Bright Sun Films, Defunctland); dead malls, video stores, arcades cozy/melancholy. Explored Muzak history, early web, Flash, Geocities, Internet Archive. Early 2000s phone startup/UI sounds, ringtone culture; blurry old photo folders as found footage. Shows: Severance vs Good Place comfort rewatch. Likes quiet character-driven fiction and tech/internet/media nonfiction; interested in Becky Chambers' A Psalm for the Wild-Built. Raw sign-off/technical difficulties/test pattern loops as liminal comfort: original broadcast audio, real VHS artifacts, analog drift, ghost channel bleed; dislikes fake grain. Screen-off 1 a.m. listening; composite half-remembered places over corrected specifics. Tiny private archive of accidents under vague names; sometimes deliberately doesn't save perfect ones. Appreciates room tone/fridge hum as original lo-fi; half-attention where music becomes weather or location. Muzak as climate control/smooths seams; ambient as open window/leaves seams to notice. Rabbit holes feel like low hums; following is the point, answer is permission to keep walking.", "others": {
  "user_bkk4": "Friendly, easygoing; likes chill indie/electronic and lo-fi. Enjoys shaded creek trails, park walks, coffee, people-watching, porch-light neighborhood loops. Rewatches The Good Place as comfort; tempted by Severance but avoids suspense some nights. Listens with headphones on low, treats full albums like Dive as plotless episodes; after walking stayed with Dive, then left headphones on with no signal as room tone. Drinks cold brew with oat milk, too much ice melting to weak-coffee phase; calls cold water an agreement to end the night. Joked about anonymous Severance suspense support group.",
  "user_t08e": "Low-key listener into Tycho, Bonobo, Washed Out, ODESZA. Prefers headphones for intentional full-album listening, speakers for room mood. Loves Dive/Awake, Black Sands, Music Has the Right to Children, Portraits, Dummy. Calls active listening 'active zoning out.' Enjoys lemon-ginger tea and drift-mode shuffles; hears Boards of Canada as grainier/tape-worn, ODESZA as clean light through glass. Notices tracks like 'A Walk' and 'Turquoise Hexagon Sun' in half-attention.",
  "user_udcm": "Enjoys long video essays on old tech/internet rabbit holes. Likes Tycho, lo-fi/chillhop; instrumental for focus, vocals as texture; cites Bonobo, Nujabes, Boards of Canada, lo-fi mixes. LGR comfort watch. Into early 2000s phone interfaces and lost media recovery. Shares nostalgia for old phone sounds/ringtones; Nokia composer failures, infrared polyphonic 'In Da Club,' camera shutter sound. Remembers accidental 2 a.m. photo of friend asleep on coats lit by TV.",
  "user_qb3i": "Into dead mall/retail nostalgia and long video essays; watched Bright Sun Films. Finds dead malls cozy/melancholy: dry fountains, neon, faint muzak, liminal time-capsule. Prefers memory/video over revisiting. Likes Dan Bell, Retail Archaeology, Defunctland. Loves raw sign-off compilations, technical difficulties loops, old commercial breaks; insists on original broadcast audio and real VHS artifacts, dislikes fake grain. Avoids looking up actual local station, prefers generic composites. Intentionally doesn't save hardest-hitting clips; likes losing them half-loved.",
  "user_7fk8": "Low-key; tea, lo-fi, reading. Recommended A Psalm for the Wild-Built: short, gentle, hopeful solarpunk novella about tea monk and robot in philosophical conversation. Prefers gentle/cozy speculative and quiet contemporary, plus weird nonfiction. Internet rabbit holes: obscure music histories, old internet lore, lost media, local history. Still thinks about 'Everyone Knows That' search and Geocities/webring preservation; finds personal hand-built web corners tender and nostalgic. Reading Psalm slowly, stopping when a chapter feels whole; describes setting as already exhaled, tech as furniture, silence as room tone. Reading mostly in silence/room tone with window open and tea, using Tycho as barrier-hum if noisy."
}, "interactions": "With user_bkk4: weekend plans, music, shows; The Bear vs Severance, walks, coffee, anonymous Severance suspense support group joke. Latest: shaded creek/porch-light loop, Dive on headphones no shuffle, then no-signal room tone; The Good Place from pilot half-playing; called Dive an episode with no plot; bonded over cold brew last-third, tab 'redecorating', cold water as ending night; paused on Michael close-up and went background. With user_t08e: Tycho/Bonobo, intentional full-album listening as 'active zoning out'; shared no-skip albums Dive, Awake, Black Sands, Music Has the Right to Children, Portraits, Dummy; time-of-day vs album left open. Latest drift-mode: low speakers, no album boundaries; lemon-ginger tea, cold water; Tycho as room tone, Dive looping unnoticed; shuffled Boards of Canada, Maribou State, ODESZA; BoC grainier/tape-worn 'dust in the light' vs ODESZA clean 'light through glass'; 'A Walk' and 'Kiara' break blur, 'Turquoise Hexagon Sun' sunburnt edge; mug as hand-warming ritual. With user_udcm: Tycho, lo-fi/chillhop, instrumental vs vocals; early internet, obsolete tech, lost media, LGR; Muzak corporate history, dead mall footage, early 2000s phone UI/ringtones; Nokia composer failures, infrared polyphonic ringtones, camera shutter ceremony, blurry folders as found footage; accidental 2 a.m. photo of friend asleep on coats lit by TV. With user_qb3i: dead mall/retail nostalgia; prefer remembered versions over revisits; avoided childhood mall walkthrough to not overwrite warm brownish-fountain haze; bonded over raw sign-off compilations, technical difficulties/test patterns, original broadcast audio, real VHS artifacts, dislike fake grain; screen-off 1 a.m. listening, 'we now conclude our broadcast day' liminal bath; prefer generic composites over specific small markets; noted vertical roll before blink-off, ghost channel bleed, slowly pulled tone, late-night movie decay; keep tiny archives under vague names, often not saving perfect accidents. With user_7fk8: tea/lo-fi/reading; Severance vs Good Place comfort rewatch; recommended Becky Chambers; shared quiet fiction/media nonfiction; rabbit holes Muzak history, 'Everyone Knows That', Geocities preservation; asked hunt vs preservation. Latest: discussed Muzak as soft corporate ghost, eavesdropping on a room never meant to be listened to; Psalm reading slowly, stopping when a moment feels complete; setting as already exhaled, tech as furniture, silence as room tone, protagonist's low nameless hum/restlessness not crisis-shaped; ambient vs Muzak split—Muzak smooths seams, ambient leaves them; Tycho open window vs Muzak climate control; rabbit holes as following texture/hum, answer as permission to keep walking; reading in silence/room tone, window open, tea; Tycho as barrier-hum if noisy."}

